  "summary": "These guidelines: (a) enable the smooth implementation of and transition to IFRS 9 in the banking sector to continue enhancing market discipline, transparency, and consistency of application and facilitate greater comparability across the banking sector by detailing supervisory expectations, especially in areas where banks are expected to exercise significant judgment or elect to use simplifications and other practical expedients permitted under standards; and (b) are not limited to loan portfolios but also apply to other financial instruments in banks' portfolios, including investments in securities (bonds and bills), other receivables, commercial papers, and derivatives.",
